rd API require their own acceptance. Reject the following false substitutes: A parameterized SELECT returning typed rows proves no commit/rollback path. Transaction metadata or a named commit export does not execute the transaction. Retry must follow declared isolation, idempotency and provider failure policy; it is not an invented retry allowance. Retain the standard rendering boundary that distinguishes escaped text, trusted markup, binary media and native views, and enforces the selected sink's trust policy. Actual web DOM/render-event execution is one qualified consumer; native/terminal/media adapters have their declared target rules. Reuse actual adapter checks without treating a web-only unsafe-DOM fixture or public rendering API inventory as universal rendering conformance. Reject the following false substitutes: A typed render export alone does not reject unsafe markup at an actual sink. HTML escaping is not a universal native-view, media or terminal trust rule. An event/schema fixture does not establish the rendering kind distinction or adapter invocation. ",
